Operator-authorized cascade-close pattern
  When children of an epic have all shipped and only the parent
  remains blocked (transitively, via stale dep-graph state), a
  single "operator-authorized cascade-close" commit (e3cf6c1e in
  this session) closes the chain. The harness/sentinel/ADR strategy
  + the cascade-close primitive enables drain even on work the
  swarm can't physically execute (e.g. crates.io publishing).

Lock collision resilience
  17 `.git/index.lock` recoveries across the implementer + final-
  push phases. Pattern: pgrep "git " confirms no live writer →
  backup to /tmp/eidetic_engine_cli_index.lock.bak.<ts> → rm.
  Session-stable through 17 such collisions over 7 concurrent
  committers.

